--- body ---
## Context

IDH skills `verify-gate` and `raid` append log lines to ticket files directly
(e.g., `bump verify-reroll`, `bump circuit-breaker`). Routing these through
the binary eliminates permission friction (IDH/0057).

`erg close` already appends a log entry as a side-effect. A general-purpose
`erg log` command covers the remaining append-only mutation sites.

## Actions

Implement `erg log <id> <line> [dir]`:
- Find ticket file by 4-digit ID in dir (default: `tickets/`)
- Append line to the log section: `{ISO8601} {line}`
  (timestamp prepended automatically; caller provides actor + verb + detail)
- Output: `LOGGED`

## Exit criteria

- `erg log 0042 "claude bump circuit-breaker — agent timeout"` appends a
  correctly formatted log line to ticket 0042
- Timestamp is ISO8601 UTC at minute precision
- Command is idempotent-safe (two calls with same line produce two entries —
  log is append-only by design)
- Test: log a line, grep for it in the ticket file
